-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party code
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

nnunet_infer.py re-implements the PlainConvUNet network and the inference
procedure (CT normalization, sliding-window prediction with Gaussian weighting
and mirroring, fold ensembling) of nnU-Net v2 so that nnU-Net checkpoints can
be loaded without installing nnU-Net. Module names follow
dynamic_network_architectures so checkpoints load unchanged.

  nnU-Net                       https://github.com/MIC-DKFZ/nnUNet
  dynamic_network_architectures https://github.com/MIC-DKFZ/dynamic-network-architectures
  Copyright German Cancer Research Center (DKFZ), Division of Medical Image Computing
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

  Isensee, F., Jaeger, P. F., Kohl, S. A., Petersen, J., & Maier-Hein, K. H. (2021).
  nnU-Net: a self-configuring method for deep learning-based biomedical image
  segmentation. Nature Methods, 18(2), 203-211.

